This is a method for getting an arbitrarily large number of spellbooks.  It
assumes that you have a working polypile, and a decent number of tools on that
pile.

For this, you will need:
Lots of bags of tricks (or wands of create monster, etc...)
Polymorphing (1 charge)
A pick axe or spell of force bolt
A cockatrice corpse

Method:
First, find a hallway that is at about 6 squares from any room or another
hallway.  Pick a square and stay there.
Now, wield the cockatrice corpse (don't forget to wear gloves first!!) and
start creating monsters.
Stay where you are, and hit any monsters next to you with the corpse.  They
will turn into statues (petrification-resistant monsters should just be 
killed with your primary weapon).
When there are no more monsters coming at you, or when the cockatrice corpse
has rotted away, you will have 2 piles of statues, one on either side of you.
Move to the far left or right of those piles and hit them both with one
polymorph spell (or wand).  
Now, break open the statues by firing one force bolt at the statues from the
same position, or break them open one by one with a pick-axe.

Now... Take these spellbooks and put them on your polypile.  For this to work,
you need to be able to identify all the spellbooks by learning the spells.
Once you know all the spells, you can pull spellbooks of genocide and 
polymorph off the pile.  Each genocide spellbook is usually good for 2 spell
castings (with HARD on) and each polymorph is usually good for 3 spells.
With genocide spellbooks, genocide everything that is no longer useful 
(elves and soldiers (if you don't need armor), jellies, insects, and annoying
monsters (rust monsters, zruties, mumakils, etc...).  Eventually, the only
creatures left could be nymphs (potions and tools), trolls (resurrection means
free prizes, sometimes), cockatrices (for more spellbooks), and creatures
that can't be genocided.  This will mean that you get even more tools (to 
create more monsters) and more cockatrices (so that you can make statues).
Presently, I have about 100 spellbooks with this method, and no longer rely
on wands of polymorph for polymorphing, using the spellbooks instead.  

